1
00:00:00,589 --> 00:00:05,429
(Prof Crawley(arriving):)Why be polite to the world's leading
expert on the dung beetle?

2
00:00:05,969 --> 00:00:08,849
(Sheldon:)Excuse me,
are you Professor Crawley?

3
00:00:09,389 --> 00:00:10,929
(Prof Crawley:)Who wants to know?

4
00:00:11,975 --> 00:00:14,395
(Sheldon:)I'm Dr. Cooper,
from the Physics Department.

5
00:00:14,561 --> 00:00:17,061
(Prof Crawley:)-Couldn't wait, huh?
-I'm sorry?

6
00:00:17,230 --> 00:00:20,770
(Prof Crawley:)I haven't even packed yet
and you're already measuring my lab...

7
00:00:20,942 --> 00:00:23,902
(Prof Crawley:)...for one
of your godless laser machines.

8
00:00:25,405 --> 00:00:28,575
(Howard:)No, you don't understand.
We just wanna ask you a question.

9
00:00:29,576 --> 00:00:31,456
(Prof Crawley:)Let me ask you one first.

10
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:34,710
What's a world-renowned entomologist
with a doctorate...

11
00:00:34,873 --> 00:00:37,543
(Prof Crawley:)...and 20 years of experience,
to do with his life...

12
00:00:37,709 --> 00:00:41,379
(Prof Crawley:)...when the university cuts off
the funding for his lab, huh?

13
00:00:42,005 --> 00:00:46,055
(Raj:)Ask rhetorical questions
that make people uncomfortable?

14
00:00:47,010 --> 00:00:48,340
[CHUCKLES]

15
00:00:49,471 --> 00:00:50,761
(Prof Crawley:)What's your deal?

16
00:00:50,931 --> 00:00:55,481
(Prof Crawley:)Are they planning to outsource my job
to Bangalore?

17
00:00:56,895 --> 00:00:58,525
(Raj:)I'm from New Delhi.

18
00:00:58,939 --> 00:01:02,279
-We should find another entomologist.
-We're here. Let's settle this.

